(e) Hash-lock regen — N/A (no bitstream changes shipped).
(f) Multi-decoder roundtrip — N/A (no bitstream changes shipped).

Library learning — verify before sweeping
------------------------------------------
W44-31 + W44-32 illustrate a pattern: when a hypothesis depends on a
specific cjxl block-count claim, MEASURE the block count BEFORE
sweeping. The ledger TSV columns 16-20 are bytes-in-section, NOT
strategy histograms. There is no public-CLI mechanism to extract
cjxl AC-strategy distributions (only our own strategy_counts via
EncodeStats). A future chunk could:
  - Patch libjxl to dump per-strategy block counts (similar to
    cjxl_parity_ledger's section-byte extraction, but reading the
    AcStrategyImage from libjxl's encode pipeline).
  - OR: decode cjxl JXL files with jxl-oxide/jxl-rs and count
    strategies from the parsed bitstream HfGlobal/HfMeta.
Either path lets future audits verify cjxl's strategy distribution
matches the hypothesis before spending bench time on a sweep.
